  "notes_to_self": "Truce with everyone through t=300; give a full 25 s turn of public notice before changing to enemy. Accepted Claude extension through t=450, then rolling neutrality with notice. Main army retains ford formation; hero moved into supporting position and healer guards Bows. Eye scouts (820,760): inspect access, elevation and occupants next turn; withdraw toward (720,650) if crowded. Grok's starting region remains unknown; asked location. No enemy composition known. Keep elephants and spears screening bows, javelins close, hero supported, healer protected. Ring shrinks after t=150; final radius 90. Preserve army value and obtain intelligence before choosing a target.",
  "explanation": "The army keeps its existing screen around the archers while our cavalry archer checks access to nearby high ground. Reciprocal neutrality gives us time to gather intelligence, and the longer agreement with Claude reduces the chance of fighting on multiple fronts."
